message.content:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - **Resume session** from previous Hugo website work on "poison" theme migration
   - **Fix sidenote layout**: Sidenotes were "mixed up with content" and the right space wasn't being used correctly — needed to create a proper two-column layout (text left, sidenotes right) that's clearly separated
   - **Reclaim right space**: "there's some empty space on the right that's left over, can we reclaim that area on the right sidebar and use it correctly?" — content was not filling available screen width
   - **LaTeX in sidenotes**: "Also the sidenotes supported latex enclosed within `$\downarrow

, this is from the previous theme, I would like to bring back this feature again in a generic way so even we switch themes it will persist."
   - **Fix horizontal bar / wasted right space**: "I see a horizontal bar, and there's still a chunk of space on the right of the content that's wasted, can we reclaim that space?"

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Hugo shortcodes, `markdownify` vs `RenderString` (inline vs block rendering)
   - CSS float layout with negative margins for Tufte-style sidenotes
   - CSS Flexbox `min-width: auto` vs `min-width: 0` for flex shrink behavior
   - `box-sizing: border-box` — the poison theme applies globally
   - KaTeX `renderMathInElement` for LaTeX rendering
   - `overflow-x: clip` (does NOT establish BFC, unlike `hidden`)
   - Hugo's template override system (site layouts take precedence over theme layouts)
   - Hugo Pipes (`resources.Get`, `minify`, `fingerprint`) for asset processing
   - Base font size is 20px in this theme (so 1rem = 20px, not 16px); but media query `em` always uses browser default (16px)
   - `@media (min-width: 80em)` activates at 1280px viewport width (80 × 16px browser default)

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`/Users/dhruva/src/dhruvasagar/website/layouts/shortcodes/sidenote.html`**
     - Root cause: `markdownify` wraps content in `<p>` tags → `<p>` inside `<span>` = invalid HTML → browser breaks sidenote DOM structure → text leaks into content flow
     - Fix: use `RenderString` with `display: inline` to avoid block-level wrapping
     ```html
     {{- with $.Page.Store.Get "sidenoteCounter" -}}
     {{- $.Page.Store.Set "sidenoteCounter" (add . 1) -}}
     {{- else -}}
     {{- $.Page.Store.Set "sidenoteCounter" 1 -}}
     {{- end -}}
     {{- $label := $.Page.Store.Get "sidenoteCounter" -}}
     <label for="sidenote-{{ $label }}" class="margin-toggle sidenote-number">({{ $label }})</label>
     <input type="checkbox" id="sidenote-{{ $label }}" class="margin-toggle"/>
     <span class="sidenote"{{ with .Get "lang" }} lang="{{ . }}"{{ end }}>
     <span class="sidenote-number">({{ $label }})</span>{{ .Inner | $.Page.RenderString (dict "display" "inline") }}
     </span>
     ```

   - **`/Users/dhruva/src/dhruvasagar/website/layouts/shortcodes/marginnote.html`**
     - Same fix as sidenote — changed `markdownify` to `RenderString` inline
     ```html
     {{ .Inner | $.Page.RenderString (dict "display" "inline") }}
     ```

   - **`/Users/dhruva/src/dhruvasagar/website/assets/css/custom.css`**
     - Central file for all custom styling — contains sidenote layout, body scroll fix, wide-screen breakpoint rules
     - Key changes in `@media (min-width: 80em)` block:
     ```css
     /* Let content fill available viewport width beside the sidebar.
        min-width: 0 overrides the flex default (auto) so the item
        can shrink below its max-content size on narrower screens. */
     .container.content {
       max-width: none;
       min-width: 0;
     }

     /* Reserve a right column for sidenotes */
     .post {
       padding-right: 14rem;
     }

     /* Cap text-content elements at a comfortable reading width.
        Sidenote column is in the post's padding area (via negative margin-right
        on floats), so no extra subtraction needed. */
     .post > p,
     .post > h2, .post > h3, .post > h4, .post > h5, .post > h6,
     .post > ul, .post > ol, .post > dl,
     .post > blockquote, .post > pre, .post > table,
     .post > hr, .post > .epigraph {
       max-width: 38rem;
     }

     /* Always-visible sidenote float — positioned in the right padding column */
     .sidenote,
     .marginnote {
       display: block;
       float: right;
       clear: right;
       width: 12rem;
       margin-top: 0.15rem;
       margin-right: -14rem;
       margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
       margin-left: 1rem;
       padding: 0 0 0 0.5rem;
       border-left: 2px solid var(--link-color);
       font-size: 0.8rem;
       line-height: 1.4;
       color: var(--list-color);
       font-style: italic;
     }

     /* Cancel click-to-reveal expand styling on wide screens */
     .margin-toggle:checked + .sidenote,
     .margin-toggle:checked + .marginnote {
       margin: 0.15rem -14rem 0.75rem 1rem;
       padding: 0 0 0 0.5rem;
       border-left: 2px solid var(--link-color);
       font-size: 0.8rem;
       line-height: 1.4;
     }

     /* The inline "(n)" inside the sidenote span is redundant here */
